window.docContents[180].resolve({"/Verified-Symbolic-and-Continuous-Computation/#PDEAtlas--Verified-Symbolic-and-Continuous-Computation--Using-Verified-Computation--Choosing-an-Interface":{"contents":"Most users should stay in ordinary Lean notation and choose an interface by\nwhat they are trying to do:\n\n* Use #cas [...] expression while exploring. It calculates and prints the\n  inferred domain and result, registering auxiliary theorems for its proof\n  evidence.* Use bare cas, or cas using h with a domain hypothesis, when an ordinary\n  theorem goal should be closed by algebraic reasoning, checked\n  differentiation, or a supported integral rule.* Use cas_nf to transform a supported real expression inside a larger goal\n  or hypothesis, or inside a selected conv occurrence. The reflected\n  Verified.Expr.eval interface remains available.* Use cega using certificate when a proof already has an enclosure, error,\n  quadrature, or residual certificate and needs its sound theorem. Bare\n  cega projects a matching checked certificate or infers a rational box from\n  local hypotheses.* Use cega [enclose x in [a, b]] e when an EnclosedOn, BoundOn, or\n  ApproxOn goal over an exact rational box, or an ordinary inequality in the\n  box variables, should be closed by a fresh interval certificate; the goal\n  selects the projection. Prefix (prec := n) or (depth := n) when the\n  default policy is too coarse.* Use cas? or cega? when the same proof search should also explain the\n  selected route in the InfoView.* Use bare cega for a numerical bound on an interval integral with a closed real\n  integrand and rational limits. It accounts for the quadrature error as well as sample\n  uncertainty.* Use the lower-level Verified.Expr and certificate constructors only when\n  extending the engine or building a reusable verified algorithm.\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Verified Symbolic and Continuous Computation\u0009Using Verified Computation","header":"10.5.1. Choosing an Interface","id":"/Verified-Symbolic-and-Continuous-Computation/#PDEAtlas--Verified-Symbolic-and-Continuous-Computation--Using-Verified-Computation--Choosing-an-Interface"}});